  "comboAudit": "Anchor set: every anchor is sound-initial + spelling-initial (or documented medial for gn/gli) from the illustrated library. All noun/themeDir pairs are manifest-proven via the sound-boxes-bank-it + blending-board-deck-it harvest EXCEPT isola/island/beach — curl-verified live 200 (2026-07-16, https://www.lessoncraftstudio.com/image-library-webp/themes/beach/island@2x.webp); igloo/winter also verified 200 as fallback but isola is the native alfabetiere choice. c tile = suono duro /k/ (casa); g tile = suono duro /g/ (gatto); soft ce/ci/ge/gi values are taught in the blending decks, not on single tiles. gn and gli use MEDIAL anchors (a-gnello, coni-glio): gnomo is not in IMAGE_VOCABULARY and word-initial gli- collides with the article. extraWords: 299 high-frequency classe-prima words (articoli, giorni-scuola verbs in io/tu/lui forms, family, classroom, animals, colors, numbers 1-10), hand-swept for profanity/anatomy/alcohol — sei/sette kept (numbers), sedere/seno/peto-class words excluded, vino/birra excluded and neverSpeak'd. neverSpeak covers the vulgar/scatological/anatomy surfaces buildable from the tray (cacca/pipì/culo/cazzo-class) so nonwordTTS never voices them. nonwordTTS true: Italian orthography is transparent — TTS reads pseudowords cleanly, which is pedagogically wanted (parole inventate prove real decoding).",
  "notes": "it tray = 21 native letters + j/k/w/x/y as quiet GUEST tiles (guest:true — ignored by the tool, kept quieter in the tray so foreign names like Jeep, kiwi, yogurt stay buildable without claiming an Italian sound) + accented vowels à è é ì ò ù as quiet vowel tiles (needed for è, sì, più, perché, città, può, papà — core classe-prima words) + 5 digraph tiles of the metodo fono-sillabico: ch (suono duro: chiave), gh (suono duro: ghianda), gn (agnello, medial), gli (coniglio, medial), sc (/ʃ/ davanti a e-i: sciarpa). h alone = quiet tile (only in ho/hai/ha and in the che/chi ghe/ghi chunks); q = quiet tile (q si usa solo con la u: quadro is built q-u-a-d-r-o). Doppie are built with two single tiles (g-a-t-t-o) — the sound-boxes tool owns the one-long-sound teaching moment. The number word uno is listed once (article and number share the form)."
